  "solution": {
    "text": "1. In polar aprotic solvent, primary alkyl halides undergo <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>S</mtext> <mtext>N</mtext> </msub> <msup> <mrow></mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msup> </mrow> </math> reaction with <math> <mrow> <mtext>KCN,</mtext></mrow> </math> to give alkyl nitrile.<br /><br />2. Alkyl nitriles, reduce in presence of <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>H</mtext> <mtext>2</mtext> </msub> <mo>/</mo><mtext>Pd,</mtext></mrow> </math> give <math> <mrow> <msup> <mtext>1</mtext> <mtext>o</mtext> </msup> <mo>&#8722;</mo></mrow> </math> amines.<br /><br />3. Cyclic ketones, on reduction with <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>H</mtext> <mtext>2</mtext> </msub> <mo>/</mo><mtext>Pd,</mtext></mrow> </math> form <math> <mrow> <msup> <mtext>2</mtext> <mtext>o</mtext> </msup> <mo>&#8722;</mo></mrow> </math> alcohol.<br /><br /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e8d4fe47-5190-4caa-a692-16c5551bd271-image17.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 126px;\" /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/ae380bb4-3187-4028-b10a-4b9af5766ac2-image18.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 210px;\" /><br /><math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math> reduces <math><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> into <math><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>",
